1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
东北老话：猪肉炖粉条，馋死野狼嚎
A Dongbei rhyme: this stew makes wolves howl

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:04,400
主角不是肉，是这把宽粉条
The star isn't the meat — it's the wide noodles

3
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:06,600
满族人为了耐寒耐饥
The Manchus wanted to beat cold and hunger

4
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:08,800
把土豆做成粉条，和肉同炖
So they made potato noodles, stewed with pork

5
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,000
五花肉出油，粉条最会吸
Pork belly renders fat, the noodles drink it up

6
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,200
一夹，颤巍巍挂满汤汁
Lift one — it trembles, glazed in broth

7
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:15,400
讲究的，还要加一把酸菜
The classic version adds pickled cabbage

8
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:17,600
它和"杀猪菜"，是同一个根
It shares a root with the pig-slaughter feast

9
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:19,800
从清代满族祭祀的还愿肉演变来
Evolved from a Qing-era Manchu ritual dish

10
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:22,000
最普通的一锅，最下饭
The plainest pot — and the most rice-devouring

11
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,200
一句顺口溜，记住一整锅乡愁
One rhyme holds a whole pot of home

12
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:26,200
炖粉条放酸菜还是不放？评论区见
Pickled cabbage in your stew, or not?

13
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:28,300
下集完结：姑爷进门，小鸡为啥"断魂"
Finale: why the chicken meets its doom
